---
// Proof-point stat band: three numbers a newcomer can grasp at a glance,
// each caption naming its number in the first breath. Not a tier readout.
---

<section class="cql-stats">
  <div class="cql-container">
    <div class="cql-stats__grid">
      <div class="cql-stat">
        <div class="cql-stat__value"><span class="cql-stat__num">~96%</span></div>
        <div class="cql-stat__caption">
          costQL predicts how much work a query takes, and its estimate is about 96% accurate.
          <span class="cql-stat__guarantee">The price you bill on is a safe max, never below the real work.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cql-stat">
        <div class="cql-stat__value"><span class="cql-stat__num">~90</span><span class="cql-stat__unit">lines</span></div>
        <div class="cql-stat__caption">
          About 90 lines of adapter teaches costQL a brand-new API. The engine never changes.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cql-stat">
        <div class="cql-stat__value"><span class="cql-stat__num">1</span><span class="cql-stat__unit">file</span></div>
        <div class="cql-stat__caption">
          Every quote comes from one small file you ship with your app. No server, no network call.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cql-stats__note">
      Measured on three real GraphQL APIs, priced fully offline. <a href="#tiers">How the fidelity tiers work →</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
